  "prompt": "Build an original dependency-free static slider matching v4 tile 89:217 in a372×264 Stage. Use a324×168 native plane at reference origin24,20 and a400×520 full composition with the complete368×320 original model and all original copy. Preserve the240×64 three-well plate including its284×108 shadow root,all40px wells,and the three40px orange head/glint pairs. The reference head at256,110 approaches the third well at272,112; reduced starts at the exact supplied checkpoint. The two supplied afterimages retain parent alpha1/12 and1/6 with80/40ms histories and450/150px-per-second authored prehistory. Roll highlights without rotating shadows. At rest,native inter-well changes launch a bounded vertical impulse of-600*min(1,distance/80) through the same380/32/1 analytic spring; preserve cross-axis velocity during interruption. Full retains the original236px rail,three34px stations,44px numbered ball and immediate original digit feedback. Keep literal original clamps,all six/three detents,keys,Page steps,pointer rules and complete full source state. Full input proxies preserve original labels,focus and capture outside the painted planes. Retain the actual painted node in both modes when opacity-fading; clone becomes live. Use the live plane for view variables. Keep the full source field unselectable so native text drag never cancels a gesture. Source thumb paths are0.2 for Dot/Stepper and0.1 for Volume; never assume child order. Direct dragging has no transition; release uses stiffness380/damping32/mass1 with actual pointer velocity and.55 rubber-banding. Reduced changes use150ms retained opacity feedback with stable focus rings and unchanged compositing. Preserve source attribution, local fonts,44px physical hit height and at least11px optical text. Stage owns Drag and fitting; no outer panel or private replay button. Suspend independent source/view clocks under caller, document and full viewport holds; queue intent while consuming recognized keys immediately. Dispose listeners, observers, frames, actual capture, hidden geometry probes, easing samplers and retained layers. Offline exports require no runtime library or network.",
